  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'The sneaker leads to the first trick; thereafter the winner of each trick leads to the next. Players must follow suit if possible, or trump if void in the led suit; when able they must head the trick (beat the current winning card). Four tricks are played per round. Each trick won pays one quarter of the pot (Pinke); a player who joins but takes no tricks pays a bête (equal to the pot); the sneaker with only one trick pays a bête, and with zero tricks pays double bête (Mauschelbete).',
    Player: 'The sneaker leads to the first trick; thereafter the winner of each trick leads to the next. Players must follow suit if possible, or trump if void in the led suit; when able they must head the trick (beat the current winning card). Four tricks are played per round. Each trick won pays one quarter of the pot (Pinke); a player who joins but takes no tricks pays a bête (equal to the pot); the sneaker with only one trick pays a bête, and with zero tricks pays double bête (Mauschelbete).',
    objective: "Win as many tricks as possible, provided you win at least TWO if you 'Sneak', or ONE if you simply 'Play'.",
    gameplay: 'The sneaker leads to the first trick; thereafter the winner of each trick leads to the next. Players must follow suit if possible, or trump if void in the led suit; when able they must head the trick (beat the current winning card). Four tricks are played per round. Each trick won pays one quarter of the pot (Pinke); a player who joins but takes no tricks pays a bête (equal to the pot); the sneaker with only one trick pays a bête, and with zero tricks pays double bête (Mauschelbete).',
    keyRules: [
      'Forehand leads bidding: announce sneak (commit to win at least 2 tricks) or pass (drop out). If all pass, cards are thrown in and next player pays 4 chips to pot and deals.',
      'Once someone sneaks, others may pass (fold) or play along (Mitgehen). If all fold, sneaker takes pot without play.',
      'Active players may exchange up to 4 cards with the talon before play.',
      'Sneaker leads first trick; winner of each trick leads the next. Must follow suit; if void must trump; must head the trick if able.',
      'Each trick wins 1/4 of the Pinke. Joining but taking 0 tricks pays a bête (equal to pot). Sneaker with only 1 trick pays bête; with 0 tricks pays double bête (Mauschelbete).',
    ],
